msgid "This is about a device plugged in with a USB cable (or mounted in Files).\n\nWhen you plug in a Kobo, Kindle or similar reader, Bookx reads the reading progress and the highlights and notes the device keeps: from the Kobo’s own database, or from KOReader’s “.sdr” files if KOReader is installed on it. It merges them with your library. Progress only moves forward, highlights and notes are united, and nothing is deleted on either side.\n\nA Kobo needs no KOReader for this; its own reading state is read. A Kindle’s own state is not readable, only KOReader’s files. If the device has no readable state, nothing happens. Reading progress is never written to the device; notes go to it only as a new KOReader notes file where there is none.\n\nOff by default: the connection banner offers a one-time Sync. Answering it never changes this setting. Turn the switch on to sync on every connection without asking."
